From 514da1a9607795003b3dee7277112df11b082bb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu381: vp9: Clear the registers per frame

The VP9 register set lives in the context and config_registers() only
sets the fields a frame needs. The segment feature enables, the
reference scale factors and the reference strides keep the values of
earlier frames, and the loop filter deltas of the last frame are ORed
into what is already there.

Clear the register set before it is filled, as the H.264 and HEVC
backends do.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
@@ -462,6 +462,8 @@ static void config_registers(struct rkvd
 			(V4L2_VP9_FRAME_FLAG_KEY_FRAME |
 			 V4L2_VP9_FRAME_FLAG_INTRA_ONLY));
 
+	memset(regs, 0, sizeof(*regs));
+
 	regs->common.reg009_dec_mode.dec_mode = VDPU381_MODE_VP9;
 
 	regs->vp9_param.reg103.vp9_intra_only_flag = intra_only;
